load @term/seed/type/term
  find term

# The surface layer of the type system, the everyday code a person writes. It is gradual and bidirectional. Gradual
# means a type may be left unknown and filled in later, so partially typed code still runs, with the unknown type acting
# as a permissive any that the checker trusts at the boundary. Bidirectional means the checker runs in two modes that
# call each other: it checks an expression against an expected type when one is known, and otherwise synthesizes a type
# from the expression and propagates it. This is what makes the surface read like ordinary imperative code (mutable
# values, loops, records) while still inferring most annotations. The surface is the inference front end; everything it
# accepts in the functional fragment is lowered into the kernel terms and judged there, so the surface is convenient and
# the kernel is the single authority. The form carries the term being checked; the gradual unknown and the two
# checking modes are the layer's mechanism.
form surface-type
  link term, like term
